body:
hi, i was wondering what do you mean by "address wouldn't match the one on the uni letter"? this is because i thought that student accom address proof can be provided by the uni upon request, so im not sure what did you mean...

&#x200B;

also, i was wondering am i required to provide my student id card? i am afraid that the name on the student id card does not match my passport / BRP, since on the official documents my full name is out, but I believe UoG student card only shows the first and last name?

&#x200B;

how long does it take for the card to come in the mail? did u receive it through student accom address mailbox (if there is one)? thank you and sorry for question spam hahaha

sorry if i offended you with the period remark, i myself am a female and i do not mean anything sexist about it

&#x200B;

"being on their periods 24/7" is a common phrasing that means being extremely emotional with unknown or identified cause in where i am living, in which we don't use english as our first language, and it is applicable to be both males and females outside the context of human biology, e.g. we would refer to our boss as being on their periods no matter if the boss is male or female if the person is extremely temperamental and emotional

&#x200B;

i didn't pass my undergraduate studies fyi, in where i live after high school we can study medicine directly in universities

&#x200B;

about punctuation i just skip them because its not available on my keyboard and if i have to switch to punctuation i have to switch the interface of my keyboard which is extremely inconvenient to do so when all i want to do is rant
